{title: Rock of Ages}
{lyricist: Augustus M. Toplady}
{composer: Thomas Hastings}
{year: 1776}
{meta: tune-year 1830}
{key: C}
{meta: tune TOPLADY}
{meta: meter 7.7.7.7.7.7}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to TOPLADY}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags cross, refuge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Rock of Ages, [F]cleft for [C]me,
[C]Let me [G7]hide my[C]self in Thee;
[G7]Let the water [C]and the blood,
[G7]From Thy wounded [C]side which flowed,
[C]Be of sin the [F]double [C]cure;
[C]Save from [G7]wrath and make me [C]pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Not the labors [F]of my [C]hands
[C]Can ful[G7]fill Thy [C]law's demands;
[G7]Could my zeal no [C]respite know,
[G7]Could my tears for[C]ever flow,
[C]All for sin could [F]not a[C]tone;
[C]Thou must [G7]save, and Thou a[C]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Nothing in my [F]hand I [C]bring,
[C]Simply [G7]to the [C]cross I cling;
[G7]Naked, come to [C]Thee for dress;
[G7]Helpless, look to [C]Thee for grace;
[C]Foul, I to the [F]fountain [C]fly;
[C]Wash me, [G7]Savior, or I [C]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]While I draw this [F]fleeting [C]breath,
[C]When mine [G7]eyes shall [C]close in death,
[G7]When I soar to [C]worlds unknown,
[G7]See Thee on Thy [C]judgment throne,
[C]Rock of Ages, [F]cleft for [C]me,
[C]Let me [G7]hide my[C]self in Thee.
{end_of_verse}
